### Recover acquisition settings from image metadata

Exact exposure times, pixel size, z-step, laser settings, and other acquisition parameters are often stored in the original image metadata. In Fiji/ImageJ, open the raw file and use **Image > Show Info...** (or press **I**) to inspect the metadata. Copy the relevant values into your records. If you use an assistant to extract fields from metadata text, verify every value against the raw metadata before publication.

### Generated methods draft

Each different selection or acquisition reference adds a separate entry, including repeated use of the same microscope. An unchanged second click does not duplicate it. Use **Clear All** to start again. Review all placeholders and acquisition-specific settings before publication.
